rue" :answer/id #uuid "52bd3cd1-590a-5e2c-b64a-56b724b306e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true"} [:db/ensure "17592186707100-III-true" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186707100-III" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e4f8b26-3549-586d-85a8-50fc4263aa00" :answer-field/key "The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_{1}, \\mathbf{a}_{2}, \\mathbf{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent." :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox :answer-field/choices ["17592186707100-III-false" "17592186707100-III-true"] :answer-field/correct "17592186707100-III-false"} [:db/ensure "17592186707100-III" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add 17592186707100 :question/answer-fields "17592186707100-III"] [:db/retract 17592186707100 :question/answer-fields 17592186707062] [:db/cas 17592186707100 :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}+2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$.\n\nII. $x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$.\n\nIII. The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_{1}, \\mathbf{a}_{2}, \\mathbf{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent." "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [:db/cas 17592186707100 :question/worked-solution "A set is **linearly independent** when the equation $x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the solution $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$. A nontrivial solution proves **linear dependence**.\n\nTest the proposed combination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}+2\\mathbf{a}_{3}&=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\ne\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe homogeneous vector equation gives the coordinate system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1}-2x_{2} &=0 \\\\ -2x_{2}-x_{3} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nChoose one coefficient nonzero and solve the remaining coordinate equations by substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_{2}&=1 \\\\ x_{1}-2(1)&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{1}=2 \\\\ -2(1)-x_{3}&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{3}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives a nontrivial solution. Verify it directly:\n\n$$\n2\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}-2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nThe coefficients are not all zero, so the set is **linearly dependent**.\n\nA failed candidate alone does not prove independence; the homogeneous-equation argument settles the classification.\n\nStatement I is **false**. Statement II is **false**. Statement III is **false**." "A set is **linearly independent** when the equation $x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the solution $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$. A nontrivial solution proves **linear dependence**.\n\nTest the proposed combination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}+2\\mathbf{a}_{3}&=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\ne\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe homogeneous vector equation gives the coordinate system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1}-2x_{2} &=0 \\\\ -2x_{2}-x_{3} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nChoose one coefficient nonzero and solve the remaining coordinate equations by substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_{2}&=1 \\\\ x_{1}-2(1)&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{1}=2 \\\\ -2(1)-x_{3}&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{3}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives a nontrivial solution. Verify it directly:\n\n$$\n2\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}-2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nThe coefficients are not all zero, so the set is **linearly dependent**.\n\nA failed candidate alone does not prove independence; the homogeneous-equation argument settles the classification.\n\nThe statement “$\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}+2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$.” is **false**. The statement “$x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$.” is **false**. The statement “The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_{1}, \\mathbf{a}_{2}, \\mathbf{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.” is **false**."] [:db/ensure 17592186707100 :question/validate]]
